{"nodes": [{"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_one_idea_per_problem_rule", "label": "One Idea Per Problem Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shortlist at most two solutions per problem; the FINAL set keeps exactly one per problem, with the strong alternative mentioned inside that idea's card. This is a cut, not a ranking. It is why Swarm Ledger appears inside Canary Maze's card instead of as its own idea."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "label": "The P4 Decision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept Canary Maze, killed Swarm Ledger at stage `competition`. Rationale, verbatim: 'Not a judgement about which pitch reads better. The scans separated them on facts.' Mechanism novelty for the Ledger is GONE (PayPal patent, WebDecoy, a stub repo); its own core claim is falsifiable in one search and 'must be deleted, not softened'; and real demo data is BLOCKED because the one CC-BY log set pseudonymises IPs and User-Agents. The Maze's do-not-fork bucket came back EMPTY and real traffic is available within hours. Constraint carried forward: only one of S4-A / S4-B can reach the final set because both come from P4 and share the site-operator user."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_final_set_of_three_ideas", "label": "Final Set of Three Ideas", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1. S4-B Canary Maze (P4 site operator). 2. S2-A Non-existent source sweep (P2 wiki patroller). 3. S1-A Batch card (P1 OSS maintainer). The sweep was later killed by the critic's measurement on the organizers' own dump, leaving two survivors."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_paypal_patent_us12034731b2", "label": "PayPal Patent US12034731B2", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filed 2021-01-29, granted 2024-07-09. Claims grouping log entries and assigning 'a corresponding common actor identifier' persisting 'over the last 12 months' - i.e. the Swarm Ledger mechanism. The competitor that killed S4-A."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_webdecoy", "label": "WebDecoy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Markets 'JA4 as a correlation key inside a persistent actor identity' and 'fingerprints identify software. Actors identify attackers.' Commercial prior art for the Swarm Ledger mechanism."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_panopticon_stub_repo", "label": "Panopticon Stub Repo", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mshaheerjunaid/Panopticon, 1 star, 2026-08-11, already describes 'clustering on behaviour and JA4 TLS fingerprint instead of IP'. Third independent hit on the Swarm Ledger mechanism."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_zenodo_18895701_access_log_release", "label": "Zenodo 18895701 Access Log Release", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The one real recent CC-BY log set, 178,939 requests, Dec 2025. It pseudonymises IPs AND User-Agents, killing ASN, JA4, HTTP/2 SETTINGS and header order - so the 'spoofed the UA but JA4 matched' moment cannot be shown on real public data. A feasibility kill-fact for S4-A."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_logrip_arxiv_2508_03130", "label": "Logrip (arXiv 2508.03130)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Independently validates the residual wedge S4-A kept: the self-hosted / non-CDN operator segment."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_new_domain_gptbot_crawl_observation", "label": "New-Domain GPTBot Crawl Observation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A documented new-domain deployment logged 'Within minutes of deploying, GPTBot started crawling', found via XML sitemap; first 12 hours GPTBot 29,000+ requests, Googlebot 11, ChatGPT-User 1 - both ends of a crawler-to-user-agent handoff inside 12 hours. The reason Canary Maze's real data is 'available within hours'."}], "edges": [{"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_defaults_d1_swarm_discovery_crawler", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_idea_package_swarm_ledger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_paypal_patent_us12034731b2", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_webdecoy", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_panopticon_stub_repo", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_zenodo_18895701_access_log_release", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_new_domain_gptbot_crawl_observation", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_logrip_arxiv_2508_03130", "target": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/shortlist.md", "source_location": "shortlist.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_shortlist_the_p4_decision", "target": "hackath